            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0955" n="827" xml:id="pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.796/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-03T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Your telegram No. 5, February 17, 1 p.m. The Department considers that
                    representatives of the United States Government should not initiate or conduct
                    private business negotiations on behalf of private American interests with
                    foreign governments. You should not, therefore, approach the Government of
                    Venezuela in the matter as suggested. Of course the Department expects the
                    Legation to give all proper assistance to responsible American interests engaged
                    in legitimate activities in foreign countries, and you may give such assistance
                    to the representative of the interests in question.</p>
                <p>Department is informing Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
